Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='codingsession', at=datetime(2026, 9, 27, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="A coding session is the owner's tap, and the routine's brief is the fence", body='⚠️ *A coding session is the owner\'s tap, and the routine\'s brief is the fence* (2026-09-27, chain `codingsession`, `docs/CODINGSESSION-PLAN-2026-09-27.md`). The secretary only PROPOSES one (`propose_coding_session`, a `Task`: plain text, ≤ 4 KB, parsed once); `Act::CodingSession` is performed by the tap alone, through the act performer (`commands::coding::Coder`, in no record), which fires the ONE routine `[coding]` names with the task and nothing else. The session runs in the cloud with no route to the tailnet; what it may do is the routine\'s saved prompt (`docs/CODINGSESSION-ROUTINE.md`, versioned here, pasted once), and the payload arrives as untrusted data. `SUZATARY_ROUTINE_TOKEN` is read from secretspec per fire and set from Settings, never a chat. A session\'s life is the closed `coding::Session`, stepped only by `Session::step`; the poll reads `claude/` branches for a report naming the session\'s URL and never runs their code. The box never merges, builds or promotes a cloud branch: "Hand to the main session" writes one todo on the `[coding]` chain, and `scripts/deploy.sh` stays the only deploy.', rationale='Decided 2026-09-27 (chain codingsession, docs/CODINGSESSION-PLAN-2026-09-27.md).', supersedes=()))